<p> Service-Producing     96,352   96,130   96,093   93,976</p>
<p> -Transp./Utilities     6,360    6,355    6,349    6,249</p>
<p> -Wholesale Trade	 6,657    6,648    6,637    6,498</p>
<p> -Retail Trade	   21,883   21,835   21,812   21,334</p>
<p>-Finance, Insurance,</p>
<p>  and Real Estate	 7,053    7,036    7,041    6,887</p>
<p> --Services		34,883   34,771   34,765   33,661</p>
<p> --Help Supply	    2,373    2,361    2,357    2,239</p>
<p> -Government	     19,516   19,485   19,489   19,347</p>
<p>The non-farm payroll data are based on a survey of employers and the jobless rate is based on a survey of households.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected a December rise in non-farm payrolls of 192,000 and a jobless rate of 5.3 percent. They also had forecast a 0.2 percent rise in December average hourly earnings and an average workweek of 34.5 hours.</p>
<p>The household survey also indicated that December employment rose 211,000, that the labor force grew by 191,000, and the number of unemployed fell 20,000.  </p>
<p>Bureau of Labor Statistics Commissioner Katharine Abraham said in a statement that the figures in the household portion of the survey for the past year were updated for seasonal adjustment in the December report as part of annual revisions. All figures for the past year reflect those changes, including the unemployment rate.</p>
